# A copy of OpenSE4 whose folder cannot be written cannot become portable (Settings, Files;
# docs/SETUP.md "A portable copy"), as a copy installed into Program Files: played by
# tools/run_input_tests.py on a copy of the client in a read-only program folder of its own,
# without OPENSE4_USER_DIR. The switch opens a message that says why and what to do instead,
# and nothing changes: the files stay in the user folder, and the runner checks that nothing
# was made beside the program (docs/BUILDING.md "Input scripts").
# ci: fixture-data (it needs nothing but our own content: CI plays it on the test fixtures)
# portable-copy read-only
options --layout=1024x768 --size=1024x768

wait-screen front
click item:Settings in=front
click item:Files in=front
wait-for item:user-folder:system
click item:"Keep saves and settings in OpenSE4's folder"
wait-for item:window:"OpenSE4's Folder Cannot Be Used"
click item:OK
wait-gone item:window:"OpenSE4's Folder Cannot Be Used"
assert-present item:user-folder:system
